maritime trade and cultural exchange, linking China with Southeast Asia and beyond. Notably, Shantou played a pivotal role in the Opium Wars and the subsequent Treaty of Nanking in 1842, which opened it as one of the five treaty ports to foreign trade, thereby impacting international relations and trade patterns in East Asia.

